From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: B Honey <9922368+Mhsbrian@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] OPENBOOK: translator stats: log the final line on exit() too

Patch 6 logged the final "openbook-stats v1" line only at the guest's
exit_group syscall, so only a guest _exit() logged one. A guest exit(),
and a return from main (which calls it), logged none (ANAL-384's VM
test). Cause: the native bridge's guest libc replaces exit() with one
that runs the guest's __cxa_finalize and then calls the host's exit()
(frameworks/libs/native_bridge_support/android_api/libc/exit.c,
native_bridge_exit). The host's exit() ends the process with its own
exit_group, which never goes through the guest syscall path.

Init() now registers a host atexit handler when counting is on, so the
host's exit() logs the line. LogIfEnabled() becomes LogFinalLine(),
which remembers the last pid that logged: a second call in the same
process logs nothing, so a process whose exit paths meet logs once, and
a fork, vfork or raw-clone child still logs its own line. Not
guaranteed: if a CLONE_VM child logs between two calls of its parent,
the parent's second call logs again; the exit paths never call it and
keep running. The line's pid comes from the getpid syscall: bionic's
cached pid is the parent's in a child made by a guest's raw clone.

Tests: exit() logs the line with the counts, a second call logs
nothing, a child forked after its parent logged logs its own and the
parent doesn't log again, and off logs nothing. Each runs in a fork
child whose stderr (the host liblog's sink) is read back.

Co-authored-by: multica-agent <github@multica.ai>
---
 kernel_api/arm64/syscall_emulation.cc         |   7 +-
 runtime/arm64/translator_stats_test.cc        | 105 ++++++++++++++++++
 .../runtime_primitives/translator_stats.h     |  19 +++-
 runtime_primitives/translator_stats.cc        |  26 ++++-
 4 files changed, 147 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

